      "role": "user",
      "content": "yea i'll get that to u in a sec. here is the data from one of the affected nodes:\n\ntraceroute to 192.168.42.10 via lyon-edge-01:\n1  10.0.0.1 (10.0.0.1)  0.452 ms  0.448 ms  0.441 ms\n2  172.16.5.1 (172.16.5.1)  12.102 ms  85.432 ms  14.221 ms\n3  172.16.5.5 (172.16.5.5)  15.234 ms  142.890 ms  18.552 ms\n4  * * *\n5  192.168.42.10 (192.168.42.10)  12.881 ms  98.112 ms  15.334 ms\n\nping stats:\n192.168.42.10:\n5 packets transmitted, 3 received, 40% packet loss\nrtt min/avg/max/mdev = 12.881/75.423/142.890/54.122 ms\n\nthe jitter is really inconsistent. hop 2 and 3 are showing these massive spikes but then it settles back down briefly. what do u think? is this a bad cable or a bad route?",
      "source": "evaluator"
